.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-calendar-list - List meetings for a day or a range


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams calendar list [--user ]… [--date ] [--days N] [--from  --to ] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List your meetings, or a colleague's, for one day or a date range.

.PP
Days are local (--tz, or this machine's zone). Another user's calendar is
shown in full when it is shared with you; otherwise the command falls back to
free/busy, which shows only times and status (--free-busy asks for that
directly). The ID column is a short handle for the full event id, usable with
\fBteams calendar show\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every row instead of --limit

.PP
\fB--chat\fP[=false]
	resolve each Teams meeting's chat and add a Chat column

.PP
\fB--date\fP="today"
	the day to show: today, tomorrow, yesterday, YYYY-MM-DD, +Nd, -Nd or a weekday name

.PP
\fB--days\fP=1
	how many days to show from --date

.PP
\fB--free-busy\fP[=false]
	show free/busy only, even for your own shared calendars

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	first day of a range (inclusive); must be paired with --to

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--include-cancelled\fP[=false]
	also show events that were cancelled

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=200
	maximum number of rows

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	last day of a range (inclusive); must be paired with --from

.PP
\fB--tz\fP=""
	IANA time zone for the days and times (default: this machine's)

.PP
\fB--user\fP=[]
	a colleague whose calendar to include (repeatable, comma-separated; default: you)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-calendar(1)\fP
